    "title": "CI: set read-only token permissions and pin actions by SHA",
    "body": "`.github/workflows/ci.yml` has no `permissions:` key, so `GITHUB_TOKEN` gets the repository default, and `actions/checkout` keeps its credentials. The actions are pinned to mutable tags (`actions/checkout@v5`, `docker/setup-buildx-action@v4`, `docker/build-push-action@v7`, `actions/cache@v5`), and the `sagemath/sagemath:latest` and `debian:stable-slim` images are unpinned; #1853 was a `latest` update breaking the sage job. Nothing is exploitable today: CI releases nothing, and no `run:` step reads pull request data.\n\nWould you take a pull request that sets `permissions: contents: read` and `persist-credentials: false`, and pins actions and images by full SHA or digest with version comments?\n\n*Assisted-by: my usual tools (LLM, Internet, computer). Mistakes are mine.*\n",
